4de48293e9135635.text:
{
 "thought": "Both sides of the plausible ranges break the model, for the same reason, and the cause is visible in the equations. I have enough to report.",
 "answer": {
  "failure": {
   "tool": "extreme",
   "args": {
    "parameter": "capacity_0",
    "value": 5000
   }
  },
  "report": "With capacity_0 = 5000, the top of its plausible range, a band first goes negative at month 33.25 and the lowest band reaches -75856 patients; with referrals_0 = 3000 the same happens at month 34.5. The first negative month is 33.25 at dt 0.25, 0.125 and 0.0625, and the largest mass-balance gap is 3.1e-11, so this is neither a time-step artefact nor lost arithmetic: Treatments = Capacity removes patients whether or not any are waiting. Restore a limit such as MIN(Capacity, Waiting_list / Minimum_treatment_time) before the model is used for any question about capacity."
 }
}

